[size=130][u]Installation[/u][/size]

You can download the latest version via Steam client - [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3843065392]Smart Minelayer[/url]
Or you can do it via the Nexus Mods - [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/x4foundations/mods/0]Smart Minelayer[/url]

[size=130][u]Save state[/u][/size]

[b]No[/b] (removing the extension does not break saves).

[size=130][u]Usage[/u][/size]

Select a ship that carries mines or laser towers, open its [b]Behaviour[/b] on the map and choose [b]Smart Minelayer[/b]. Set [b]Target Position[/b] to a point in space, or [b]Target Object[/b] to a station or gate, and confirm. The configuration window for the first slot opens on the map.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/behaviour.png[/img][/spoiler]

In the [b]Deployable[/b] section pick the type, [b]Mines[/b] or [b]Laser Towers[/b], and the item.

In [b]Shape[/b], [b]Concentric Shapes[/b], [b]Parallel Layers[/b] and [b]Offset[/b] design the field. The window shows how many items the slot needs.

In [b]Maintenance[/b] set the [b]Replacement Threshold[/b]: the share of a slot's items that must be lost before the ship refills it, 0 for at once. [b]Restock at Other Factions' Stations[/b] lets the ship buy at stations that are not yours; a new order starts with your last choice.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/config_window.png[/img][/spoiler]

Confirm, and the ship flies to the field and lays it. For another field, select the ship, right-click a spot in space, a station or a gate and choose [b]Add Minelayer Position[/b]; up to nine slots, one tab each in the window. Picking the target of an existing slot opens that slot for a change. A new target in its [b]Behaviour[/b] adds no slot. The tab of a saved slot shows [b]Delete[/b] in place of [b]Reset[/b]: tick the box beside it first. The deleted slot's items stay in space and are no longer replaced. Deleting the last slot clears the order's target too; the ship stands by until [b]Add Minelayer Position[/b] gives it a new one.

A few fields on the map, one slot each:

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/map_concentric_circles.png[/img][/spoiler]

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/map_hexagons.png[/img][/spoiler]

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/map_sphere.png[/img][/spoiler]

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/map_cube.png[/img][/spoiler]

To look at a ship's slots, right-click it with no other object selected and choose [b]Configure Smart Minelayer[/b] under [b]Orders[/b]. If the window of its first slot was closed without a slot, the same item opens it again.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/context_menu.png[/img][/spoiler]

[size=130][u]Options[/u][/size]

An options page is available via the [b]Extension Options[/b] menu. [b]Keep Slots of a Destroyed Minelayer[/b] sets how many game hours (0 to 24, default 4) the slots of a minelayer destroyed without wingmen are kept before they are dropped; its friend/foe mines keep working either way. [b]Debug Level[/b] sets the detail of the extension's log.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-SmartMinelayer/refs/heads/main/docs/images/options.png[/img][/spoiler]

